From 672134181e29569ec4155233002ef37a3cc925f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mikkojhuttunen <mikkojhuttunen@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 17:08:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Cavity workbench: bowtie layout from real arm lengths,
 astigmatism compensation

Layout: a four-mirror ring is now drawn as a bowtie built from the real
arm lengths, crystal arm at the bottom with the pump from the left and
the opposite arm on top with the output to the right, both horizontal;
only the horizontal direction is stretched to fill the panel. Elements
carry short names, the output arrow shows the live power and
wavelength, the pump arrow the pump wavelength, and curved mirrors
their incidence angle. A note gives the fold angles the arm lengths
imply and flags when they disagree with the entered angles, or when the
arm lengths cannot close a planar ring at all. The ray overlay shows
the first three round trips only.

Astigmatism: new Compensate astigmatism button scans one incidence
angle for all curved mirrors and keeps the one with m_T = m_S, and
quotes the textbook two-mirror condition R sin(theta) tan(theta) =
L(n^2-1)/n^3 for the Brewster crystal for comparison. The incidence
angle control is labelled as setting astigmatism, the results list
gains an astigmatism check, and the model notes describe both.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
